# Third-party .repo basenames that must ship enabled=0 — the single
# authoritative list. Adding a repo means adding it here (AGENTS.md
# convention 2): validate-repos.sh hard-fails the build on any entry left
# enabled=1 OR listed here but absent from the image (a renamed upstream
# repo file must be renamed here too), and reusable-build.yml hands the
# same list to check-image-integrity.sh, which re-proves both rules on the
# chunked image's cold bytes. A '?' prefix marks an optional entry:
# enforced enabled=0 when present, tolerated when absent — for repos the
# base has shipped before and may ship again. The '?' syntax is this
# repo's own convention (no upstream equivalent; aurora keeps a plain
# inline array). A repo absent from this list is only listed, never
# enforced.
#
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored by both readers.
negativo17-fedora-multimedia.repo
tailscale.repo
vscode.repo
docker-ce.repo
mozilla.repo
1password.repo
teackot-msi.repo
fedora-cisco-openh264.repo
?fedora-coreos-pool.repo
terra.repo
terra-extras.repo
terra-mesa.repo
